{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --porcelain=v1; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go | sed -n '75,81p;112,126p'; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md | sed -n '38,48p'; rg -n 'governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes =' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\"","aggregated_output":"    75\t// captureGovernanceGit runs a Git command through the read-view generation\n    76\t// when Files belongs to one. Native and preview operations retain their\n    77\t// existing behavior when there is no governance view.\n    78\tfunc captureGovernanceGit(files Files, root, producer string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n    79\t\treturn captureGovernanceGitBounded(files, root, producer, governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes, args...)\n    80\t}\n    81\t\n   112\t}\n   113\t\n   114\tfunc captureGovernanceGitBounded(files Files, root, producer string, maxOutputBytes int64, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n   115\t\treturn captureGovernanceGitBoundedContext(files, context.Background(), root, producer, maxOutputBytes, args...)\n   116\t}\n   117\t\n   118\tfunc captureGovernanceGitBoundedContext(files Files, ctx context.Context, root, producer string, maxOutputBytes int64, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n   119\t\tfiles = FilesOrNative(files)\n   120\t\tview, viewFiles := governanceReadViewFromFiles(files)\n   121\t\tif view == nil {\n   122\t\t\treturn runGovernanceGitCommandContext(ctx, files, root, args, maxOutputBytes)\n   123\t\t}\n   124\t\tif view.operation == nil {\n   125\t\t\tview.markUnknown(producer, \"Git input has no operation-scoped generation vector\")\n   126\t\t\treturn runGovernanceGitCommandContext(ctx, files, root, args, maxOutputBytes)\n    38\t\n    39\t### Functional\n    40\t- R1: `gitMaterializedChangesForIn` and `dispatchDiskSnapshot` shall bound the bytes they read by the committed tree's blob sizes plus a 256 MiB margin, so a clean tree whose checked-out bytes stay within its stored blob bytes plus the margin is compared and snapshotted whole; materialized expansion past that (smudge or CRLF filters, populated submodules, ignored files) fails closed.\n    41\t- R2: When the bytes read exceed that budget, both shall fail closed with an error that names the budget.\n    42\t- R5: Every committed tree listing these budgets read shall be bounded in bytes (64 MiB) and time (2 minutes) before it is retained; a listing past either fails closed.\n    43\t- R4: The cleanup of a delegated review's worktree shall bound the bytes it removes by the same budget, computed from the coordinator repository for the worktree's checked-out commit when the worktree is registered, so a clean worktree of a tree past the margin is removed and a worktree grown past the budget is retained.\n    44\t- R3: The budget shall never be less than the 256 MiB margin and never more than a 4 GiB ceiling; when the committed tree cannot be listed, the disk snapshot shall use the margin alone.\n    45\t\n    46\t### Non-functional\n    47\t- A listagem da árvore com tamanhos sai do mesmo `ls-tree` que a comparação já fazia; a captura de disco faz um `ls-tree -l` a mais.\n    48\t\n25:\tgovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes = 512 * 1024 * 1024\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
